  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A fixed-length record is parsed from the characters of the record itself rather than from a string per column: a value is cut and trimmed as a range within the record, and the column reads it from there, so nothing is copied for a number, date, boolean, character, enumeration or ignored column, and a string column copies once instead of twice. Around 39% less allocation on a fixed-length read and 36% through a type mapper. IColumnDefinition gains Parse( IColumnContext?, ReadOnlySpan<char> ) and INullFormatter gains IsNullValue( IColumnContext?, ReadOnlySpan<char> ), both default interface members, so an implementation outside the library is unaffected. Source- and binary-compatible with 7.4.1.",
